[Music]  I think we tend to remember  extraordinary acts of kindness simply  because they are extraordinary the act  is a reminder to us of our common  decency our desire to help other people  to care for other people which I think  we all have as kids but as we grow older  we just kind of tend to forget there was  this one experience that I'll never  forget as a few years back and my wife  and I were in Japan  [Music]  so my wife and I decided to visit this  lovely little village in the countryside  that we'd read about and we lose track  of time realized too late that we've  missed the bus and because we're out in  the middle of nowhere there's not  another bus in time to take us to the  airport in two-hour flight  we tried to take a taxi but Tokyo was  simply too far and nobody is willing to  take us we're becoming increasingly  desperate and then just at that moment  sort of mock our desperation the heavens  opened up and it started to rain so it  was really at our lowest point when this  elderly gentleman came up to us we tried  to explain to him as best we could that  we needed to get to Haneda Airport and  we need to get there pretty quickly we  don't know if he understands a word  we're saying but ultimately he just kind  of gestures for us to follow him at this  point were you know increasingly  desperate so I figured why not whatever  you got to lose  so before long we find ourselves back at  we presumed to be his house we have no  idea what's going on at this point were  completely confused but then we go to  his driveway and what do we see in his  driveway it's a taxi the guy's a taxi  driver he offers to drive us to Haneda  great  problem solved incredible we load up our  luggage and it takes us on this  incredible drive through the countryside  through the mountains through the city  and it was like we were having our own  kind of private tour of Japan it was  amazing honestly we were a little  disappointed when I was over we get to  the airport and the most amazing thing  happens I asked him how much the fare is  and he says no no you there's no fare  I said well please you know let me at  least pay for the petrol you know you  just driven us all this way  [Applause]  he just smiles and he he waves and he  wishes us our best and he gets in his  car and he's gone it was then I realized  I didn't even know his name  [Music]  so we board the plane everything's fine  and it was all because this this random  man had seen that we needed help and it  helped us and you know that's something  that I will always remember and so you  know to our random Japanese Savior I  just want to say thank you and to say  that I will try to live by your example  try to do kindness as often as I can try  to teach my kids Grace and goodness and  kindness and charity thank you for the  reminder and thank you for that  [Music]  you

